WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:05.860
Why is Corona virus killing more men than
women at a higher rate, killing men than women?

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:11.700
Early, we had just the case numbers and death
numbers from China, and we immediately saw

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.200
a much higher rate of death for men than for
women.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:21.160
And the suggestion was that in China, culturally,
men smoke more than women.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.210
Men are much more likely to be smoking cigarets.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.830
And we know cigarets weaken your respiratory
system.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.350
They can depress your immune system.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:33.640
And because coronavirus seems to vary a lot
depending on the underlying health condition

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.800
of the person infected.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.190
Men were more likely to die in China because
men are much more likely to be smokers.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:41.000
It seemed plausible in any case.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.770
The trend, though, is continuing in a lot
of different countries and we are now seeing

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:52.210
that in Italy, men are 60 percent of the cases,
but 70 percent of the deaths.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:58.570
In South Korea, more women have tested positive,
but yet the deaths are 54 percent men.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:03.770
The U.S. so far is not releasing this detail
of a detailed level of information.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:04.960
So we don't know what's going on here.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:07.330
The U.S. should start releasing that data.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:12.850
But in total, for all countries where we have
data, men are about 50 percent more likely

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:14.710
than women to die after being diagnosed.

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:19.020
Now, remember, 50 percent can mean if women
have a 2 percent death rate.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.470
Men have a 3 percent death rate.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:21.470
That's 50 percent more.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:22.470
I don't want.

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:25.470
Well, to misunderstand the numbers around
that.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:26.800
So what's at play here?

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:32.630
The smoking issue does seem to be a factor
in possibly alcohol consumption as well.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:38.740
We have world data from five years ago and
five years ago, 36 percent of men over age

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:43.650
15 smoke where only seven percent of women
over age 15 smoke.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:44.650
That's a big difference.

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:51.350
And if indeed smoking is a essentially a co-morbidity
with coronavirus, that is important.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:56.890
Meanwhile, alcohol consumption consumption
for men is eleven liters where it's two leaders.

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:59.800
For women, that may be a factor.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:05.509
We saw that SaaS and Murs also had higher
death rates for men than women.

00:02:05.509 --> 00:02:09.780
So it seems not unique to Koven, 19.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:16.730
And there is also a general evolutionary idea
that maybe women have stronger immune responses

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:23.030
to viruses in general because of pregnancy,
essentially being living nine months of your

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:26.050
life with a foreign body inside of you.

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:29.500
It may confer some kind of survival advantage.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:32.120
There could be a hormonal element to this.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:36.420
And then also actual preexisting conditions
appear to be a factor.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:41.500
We know that preexisting conditions increase
mortality for covered patients.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.590
Check out some of the gender differences.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:48.200
Men more likely to have heart disease than
women, stroke than women.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:53.910
COPD, a lung disease and slightly more likely
to have high blood pressure.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:58.970
All of these conditions are known to increase
the death rate from coronavirus.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:05.400
So the takeaways are the death rate is remaining
higher for men than women in all of the countries

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:06.830
providing data.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:09.130
We initially heard this out of China.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:13.390
Other countries providing us this data seem
to be confirming the same thing.

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:19.280
Number two, the U.S. is not providing data
of this type and the U.S. really should start.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:21.239
So that that's the second takeaway.

00:03:21.239 --> 00:03:24.709
We're going to continue following this and
see see sort of where we come up as we get

00:03:24.709 --> 00:03:24.720
more data.

